My suggestion on cukta (not deeply thought out)

cukta   x1 is a book/physical volume containing matter/work/text x2 on
                medium x3 (not necessarily bound paper, but a physical object)

All the remaining ideas currently conveyed by cukta come under 'prosa',
'cfika', 'draci', 'pemci', and 'selfi'i', together perhaps with 'vreji', 'datni'
and sometimes 'selpau' or 'so'ormei'.

Book in the abstract: selcku (also lisri, prosa, pemso'omai, lisyso'omei)
Author: finti (be lo selcukta), but usually te cfika, te pemci, te prosa

Current definitions:
================
cfika fik     fi'a fiction  x1 is a work of fiction about plot/theme/subject
 x2/under
convention x2 by author x3

cukta     cku      book     x1 is a book about subject/theme/story x2 by author
 x3 for
audience x4 preserved in medium x5

draci              drama    x1 is a drama/play about x2 [plot/theme/subject] by
dramatist x3 for audience x4 with actors x5

finti fin     fi'i invent   x1 invents/creates/composes/authors x2 for
function/purpose x3 from existing elements/ideas x4

lisri lis          story    x1 is a story/tale/yarn/narrative about
 plot/subject/moral
x2 by storyteller x3 to audience x4

pagbu pag     pau  part     x1 is a part/component/piece/portion/segment of x2

pemci pem          poem     x1 is a poem/verse about plot/theme/subject/pattern
 x2
by author x3 for intended audience x4

